  "worked_solution": "The standard Maclaurin expansion for $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =x-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5!}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReplacing $x$ with ${x}^{2}$ in the above expansion and simplifying gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}) & =({x}^{2})-\\frac{1}{6}({x}^{2})^{3}+\\frac{1}{120}({x}^{2})^{5}+⋯ \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{6}{x}^{6}+\\frac{1}{120}{x}^{10}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
